\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  After  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Hits Record High -Source\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2010\par 04:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Adds quotes, background) \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (Dow Jones)--The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar hit an all-time high against the greenback, a person familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The person said the MAS "went in to smooth the U.S. dollar's fall around S$1.3435."\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar overnight hit a record high, with the U.S. dollar sliding to S$1.3425. The previous record was S$1.3438 to the greenback in July 2008.\par \par \uc2 "They (MAS) will continue to smooth the U.S. dollar's fall for now, but this is a regional issue with widespread weakness for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the person said.\par \par \uc2 At 0227 GMT the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.3460. It was the first time since April that MAS has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The local dollar rose after better-than-expected U.S. housing and employment data overnight eased worries about the health of the global economy, sapping demand for safe assets such as the U.S. dollar and Treasurys.\par \par \uc2 "They (MAS) expect continued weakness in the U.S. dollar. The basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the Singapore dollar trades with will likely go higher in the short term," the person said.\par \par \uc2 "If that happens the local dollar will further rise and the MAS' role will not be to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but to make sure that the rise is orderly."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses the exchange rate rather than interest rates as its main policy tool because Singapore's trade flows dwarf the island's small domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 The MAS also views the Singapore dollar's rise as part of a trend among Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after China decoupled the yuan from the U.S. dollar in mid-June, the person said. Although the yuan has barely risen, the de-pegging by the People's Bank of China paved the way for other export-reliant Asian economies to let their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain further, the person said.\par \par \uc2 The MAS aggressively tightened policy in April by raising the trading band for the Singapore dollar and targeting a "modest and gradual appreciation" for the local dollar, changing its previous policy of zero appreciation.\par \par \uc2 -By Singapore Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4150; djn.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com [ 03-09-10 0228GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100903e6930004d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
