\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2010\par 04:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF SURVEY: APRIL-JUNE CAPEX DOWN 1.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Capital investment by Japanese corporations decreased by 1.7% from year-ago levels during the April-June quarter, a survey released Friday by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed. (published 2356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: S KOREA REVISED 2Q GDP +1.4% ON QUARTER, +7.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economy grew at a slower pace than initially thought in the second quarter from the first on weaker construction sector investment, adding weight to the view that any monetary tightening for the rest of the year will be limited and gradual. (published 2349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AFTER \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR HITS RECORD HIGH -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has Friday \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar hit an all-time high against the greenback, a person familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking said. (published 0119 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOE TUCKER: PROGRESS MADE ON CAPITAL REQUIREMENTS FOR BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of England Deputy Governor Paul Tucker said Friday that the Financial Stability Board and the Basel Committee for Banking Supervision are making "substantive progress" on devising new capital and liquidity requirements for banks, "notwithstanding what has been in the press." (published 0201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PERFORMANCE OF SERVICES INDEX UP 0.9 PTS IN AUGUST VS JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's services sector was sluggish in August as political uncertainty and the steady withdrawal of fiscal stimulus damped activity. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA GAS PLANS TO RAISE $300 MLN VIA OCTOBER BOND ISSUE -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Gas Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to raise $300 million by issuing Swiss franc-denominated bonds in October to fund its overseas \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a company official said Friday. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE MANUFACTURING PMI FALLS, SIGNALS GLOBAL UNCERTAINTY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's manufacturing activity contracted in August after expanding for 15 straight months, suggesting global economic uncertainties may be taking a toll on the island nation after its incandescent growth in the first half of the year. (published 0005 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =TAKING STOCK: HOMEBUILDER ETF SUGGESTS HOUSING DOWNTREND ENDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Before the housing market can start getting better, it first has to stop getting worse. Based on the homebuilder sector's recent performance, the bottom may have already been seen. (published 2014 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =RATE FUTURES REPORT: OPEN INTEREST DROP SIGNALED SELLOFF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some traders had an inkling of the impending selloff of long-term Treasury futures a few days ago even as the December 30-year Treasury bond contract climbed to a contract high. (published 2023 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-09-10 0205GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100903e6930003r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
