\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Singapore Dollar Rises To New Record Vs US Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2010\par 02:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from trader, background on U.S. data)\par \par \uc2 By Gaurav Raghuvanshi\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose to its highest level ever overnight after better-than-expected data from the U.S. helped ease economic fears and investors returned to assets linked to growth such as equities and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.3457 at 2359 GMT Thursday, or Friday morning in Asia, after falling as low as S$1.3425 overnight. The previous record intraday low for the greenback was S$1.3438, touched on July 15, 2008.\par \par \uc2 A person close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should the greenback reach around S$1.3440.\par \par \uc2 Officials of the MAS weren't immediately available for comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The latest bout of better-than-forecast U.S. housing and employment data have eased worries about the health of the economy, sapping demand for safe assets such as the U.S. dollar and government Treasurys. The market now awaits U.S. non-farm payrolls data due later in the day, which will have a strong impact on the U.S. dollar's performance.\par \par \uc2 "The Singapore dollar will continue to trade heavy because global risk appetite has improved. There may, however, be a bit of consolidation ahead of the U.S. non-farm payrolls data due tonight," said a trader at an international bank.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar may find support near S$1.3440 and face resistance at S$1.3500, he said.\par \par \uc2 The National Association of Realtors Thursday said its index for pending sales of used homes increased 5.2% to 79.4 in July, surprising economists, who had tipped a decline. Initial jobless claims declined by 6,000 to 472,000 in the week ended Aug. 28.\par \par \uc2 The reports, along with Wednesday's upbeat manufacturing report out of the U.S. and China, provided relief for investors. Recent data had come in weaker than expected, raising fears of a double-dip recession and deflation.\par \par \uc2 -By Gaurav Raghuvanshi; Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 154; gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com [ 03-09-10 0020GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100903e6930000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
