\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ MAS To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  If  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Returns To Record High -Source\b0\par\par\uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2010\par 09:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 2 Sep 2010 03:00 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  MAS 'On \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Watch' - Source\par \par \uc2 2 Sep 2010 03:00 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  Dollar Trading Around 2% Above MAS Band Midpoint -Source\par \par \uc2 2 Sep 2010 03:01 EDT *DJ  MAS To Tolerate Midterm Singapore Dollar Rise If Orderly, In Line With Region -Source\par \par \uc2 2 Sep 2010 03:01 EDT *DJ  MAS To Stand Pat In October 'Unless Things Change Dramatically' -Source\par \par \uc2 2 Sep 2010 03:07 EDT =DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  MAS On '\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Watch' But Ready For Stronger SGD -Source\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is poised to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the local dollar climbs back to around its record high, a person familiar with the situation said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore is prepared to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise against the U.S. dollar in the short to medium term if the move is orderly and in line with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the person told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 The MAS is "on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch," the person said.\par \par \uc2 This suggests \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be imminent for the MAS, which is thought to have stayed out of the market since April. The U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.3485 around 0706 GMT, up from the day's low of from S$1.3454 but still close to its July 15, 2008, all-time low of S$1.3438.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar, up 4% this year against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been rising along with peers like the Malaysian ringgit and the Indonesian rupiah, as Asia has rebounded strongly from the global economic crisis and the U.S. dollar has fallen on speculation the Federal Reserve will have to loosen policy further to bolster the world's biggest economy.\par \par \uc2 In recent days the Singapore dollar has been around 2% above the midpoint of the undisclosed trade-weighted band in which the MAS guides the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the person said. "Anything above that will trigger action."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses the exchange rate rather than interest rates as its main policy tool because Singapore's trade flows dwarf the island's small domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 "If the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  we trade with moves higher against the U.S. dollar, it will be futile to fight the trend," the person said. "But any movement must be orderly. If it's not, the MAS will try to stop the volatility."\par \par \uc2 The MAS also views the Singapore dollar's rise as part of a trend among Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after China decoupled the yuan from the U.S. dollar in mid-June, the person said. Although the yuan has barely risen, the de-pegging by the People's Bank of China paved the way for other export-reliant Asian economies to let their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain further, the person said.\par \par \uc2 The MAS aggressively tightened policy in April by raising the trading band for the Singapore dollar and targeting a "modest and gradual appreciation" for the local dollar, changing its previous policy of zero appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rise is dispelling the idea of a further tightening at the next policy review, in October, said the person familiar with MAS thinking. The bank will stand pat "unless things change dramatically."\par \par \uc2 Singapore's economy grew a blistering 18.8% in the second quarter from a year earlier, accelerating from 16.9% in the first quarter and after contracting last year due to the global economic crisis. The government expects the economy to grow 13%-15% for the full year.\par \par \uc2 -By Singapore Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 02, 2010 03:07 ET (07:07 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100902e6920018r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
