\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 2\b0\par\par\uc2 2,122 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2010\par 09:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA TRADE SURPLUS TRIMMED AS KEY MINING EXPORTS SLIP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's trade surplus fell well short of expectations in July despite a rise in commodity prices through the month, as exports of coal and iron contracted and the government imported six new fighter jets. (published 0322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAS ON '\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WATCH' BUT READY FOR STRONGER SGD -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is poised to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if the local dollar climbs back to around its record high, a person familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 0707 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC HU: CROSS-BORDER YUAN USE REQUIRES MORE EFFECTIVE MACRO POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The wider use of the yuan for cross-border trade and investment requires more effective, flexible and coordinated macroeconomic policies and management, People's Bank of China Vice Gov. Hu Xiaolian said in an article published in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -run China Finance magazine. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S INDEPENDENT WILKIE: TO SUPPORT LABOR GOVERNMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian independent lawmaker Andrew Wilkie on Thursday said he will back the center-left Labor party into office, in a move that delivers momentum to Prime Minister Julia Gillard's bid to form a minority Labor government after an inconclusive national election result. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN DPJ OZAWA: YEN'S RECENT SHARP RISE WARRANTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan should \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the yen's recent strength, even if unilateral action wouldn't be very effective in turning the market trend around, Japanese ruling party presidential candidate Ichiro Ozawa said Thursday. (published 0605 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN DPJ OZAWA: TO MAKE JAPAN ECON NOT DEPENDENT ON EXPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese ruling party presidential candidate Ichiro Ozawa said Thursday that if he becomes prime minister, he would aim to create an economy not dependent on exports, suggesting he would take steps to boost domestic demand. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: THAI GOVERNMENT CONCERNED ABOUT BAHT STRENGTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai government is concerned about the strength of the baht and has asked the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to closely monitor its movement, Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Thursday after a high-level emergency meeting to discuss the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW ZEALAND WELL PLACED TO DEAL WITH UNEXPECTED FISCAL SHOCKS - FIN MIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Bill English said Thursday a new International Monetary Fund report confirms that government measures to control debt have left New Zealand well-placed to deal with potential fiscal shocks, relative to other developed countries. (published 0446 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOUTH KOREA'S AUGUST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN-EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVES SLIP FROM RECORD HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fell in August from the previous month's all-time high, largely due to a decline in the value of non-dollar assets as a result of the greenback's gains, the Bank of Korea said Thursday. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA 2Q CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS MYR16.2 BLN, DOWN 42% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia had a current account surplus of MYR16.2 billion in the second quarter of 2010, a 42% decline from a year earlier, the Department of Statistics said Wednesday. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KEXIM TO MEET BOND INVESTORS IN EUROPE END-SEPTEMBER, US IN OCTOBER -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Export-Import Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or Kexim, is planning to meet investors in the Europe at the end of the month and in the U.S. next month for a potential global bond sale in the fourth quarter, a person familiar with the company's plan said Thursday. (published 0445 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: ASIAN RATES LIKELY IN HIBERNATION FOR LONGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interest rates in Asia are set to remain lower for longer as the U.S. economic recovery stumbles. (published 0502 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =CHARTING ASIA: AUSSIE MAY RISE TO CHF0.9405 IN COMING DAYS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar jumped 2.5 percent against the Swiss franc Wednesday on contrasting economic data, and looks set to advance further in coming days. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: BANK INDONESIA LIKELY TO KEEP RATE UNCHANGED - POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia will likely keep its overnight policy rate unchanged Friday after August inflation turned out to be milder than expected. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SHINHAN FINANCIAL PRESIDENT TO BE REMOVED; ACCUSED OF BREACH OF TRUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The board of Shinhan Financial Group Co. will soon meet to remove President Shin Sang-hoon from his post due to allegations of breach of trust--news that sent shares of the financial holding firm tumbling. (published 0552 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NZ FARMING SYSTEMS URUGUAY RECOMMENDS ACCEPTANCE OF OLAM OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NZ Farming Systems Uruguay\f28 \uc2 \f2  Thursday recommended shareholders accept Singapore-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Olam International\f28 \uc2 \f2 's offer of NZ$0.70 a share for the company and said it has discontinued its search for a new investor. (published 0218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NTUC FAIRPRICE, DAIRY FARM BID FOR CARREFOUR SINGAPORE, MALAYSIA ASSETS - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's \f28 \uc2 \f2 NTUC FairPrice\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Dairy Farm International Ltd. and Malaysian private equity group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Navis Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  have placed bids for French retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Carrefour SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Singapore and Malaysia assets, a person familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 0443 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: BANPU UNIT SELLS 8.72% STAKE IN INDO TAMBANGRAYA FOR $395 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banpu PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Thailand's largest coal miner by revenue, said Thursday that its wholly-owned unit has sold an 8.72% stake in Indonesian coal miner unit \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Indo Tambangraya Megah\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a deal worth $395 million. (published 0609 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANPU: RESUBMITTED CENTENNIAL BID TO AUSTRALIA'S FOREIGN REVIEW BOARD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banpu PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Thailand's largest coal miner by revenue, said Thursday it has resubmitted its application to Australia's Foreign Investment Review Board for the full takeover of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Centennial Coal Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =WSJ: FORD: 70% OF ITS GLOBAL GROWTH THIS DECADE TO COME FROM ASIA PACIFIC, AFRICA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ford Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects 70% of its global growth this decade to come from Asia Pacific and Africa, a senior executive said Thursday. (published 0629 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: GENERAL MOTORS MULLS RESTARTING INDONESIA PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Motors Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is considering restarting a production plant in Indonesia with an investment of $150 million, and a decision is expected within the next 90 days, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tim Lee\f28 \uc2 \f2 , GM's president for international \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said Thursday. (published 0531 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: GM DAEWOO ON TRACK FOR TURNAROUND THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GM Daewoo Auto & Technology Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., backed by new models, is on track to post a profit this year, reversing from the previous year's net loss, while being determined to achieving a double-digit percentage market share in the domestic market, the company's chief executive said late Tuesday. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOSTERS CFO JUMPS SHIP TO PORT, RAIL OPERATOR ASCIANO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foster's Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Financial Officer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Angus McKay\f28 \uc2 \f2  has left the beverages group and taken up the same roll at port and rail operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asciano Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the two companies said Thursday. (published 0034 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NZ COMMERCE COMMISSION ALLEGES ANTI-COMPETITIVE CONDUCT BY FREIGHT COMPANIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand Commerce Commission said Thursday that it has filed proceedings in the High Court at Auckland against a number of international freight forwarding companies on charges of colluding on surcharges and fees for air freight forwarding services to New Zealand. (published 0133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: HARUM ENERGY SETS INDICATIVE IPO PRICE AT IDR5,000-IDR6,300/SHARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Coal producer PT Harum Energy has set an indicative price of between IDR5,000 and IDR6,300 per share for its planned sale of up to a 24% stake, or 650 million shares, through an initial public offering slated for later this month, an official at one of the underwriters told reporters Thursday. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBE ASIATIQUE DEFERS IPO DUE TO WEAK GLOBAL MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine property developer Globe Asiatique Realty Holdings Corp. has decided to indefinitely postpone an initial public offering it had planned to launch on Sept. 15, citing "weak global market conditions," the Philippine Stock Exchange said Thursday. (published 0229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAN MIGUEL: MAY INVEST $8 BLN FOR POWER PROJECTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 San Miguel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that its power unit, San Miguel Energy Corp., may invest as much as $8 billion in a project that will integrate a liquefied natural gas facility with power plants. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =WSJ: BAIDU LAUNCHES APPLICATION PLATFORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Baidu Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has launched an application platform through which developers can distribute applications through a browser, Baidu Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robin Li\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday at the company's 2010 Technology Innovation Conference. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ COMMERCE COMMISSION: ALLEGES ANTI-COMPETITIVE CONDUCT BY FREIGHT COMPANIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand Commerce Commission said Thursday that it has filed proceedings in the High Court at Auckland against a number of international freight forwarding companies on charges of colluding on surcharges and fees for air freight forwarding services to New Zealand. (published 0344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FONTERRA APPOINTS ADVISERS FOR NEXT STEPS IN CAPITAL STRUCTURE CHANGES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fonterra Co-Operative Group Ltd. said Thursday that it has appointed advisers for the next step in its capital structure changes, adding that a new trading system that will allow farmers to buy and sell Fonterra shares among themselves will begin in late 2011 at the earliest. (published 0354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =CINEMAX CHAIRMAN: LOOKING TO SELL NAGPUR MALL PROPERTY FOR INR750M-INR850M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-09-10 0713GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cinemax India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is looking to sell its Nagpur mall project for INR750 million-INR850 million and will use the proceeds to repay high-cost debt and for expansion. (published 0419 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DELTA AIR LINES PRESIDENT: STRONG YEN BOOSTING PASSENGER DEMAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The president of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Delta Air Lines Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ed Bastian\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday that the strong yen is helping to boost passenger demand from Japan. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ELPIDA: HAVE DEVELOPED 4-GIGABIT NAND FLASH MEMORY WITH SPANSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elpida Memory Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Spansion Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . have developed a new flash memory chip with a simpler cell structure than existing ones, and plans to start mass production next year at its western Japan plant. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ESPRIT LAST FISCAL YEAR NET PROFIT FALLS 11% TO HK$4.23 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fashion retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Esprit Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its net profit for the 12 months ended June 30 fell 11% on weak wholesale business and continued economic weakness in Europe, which accounts for the majority of its revenue. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINOSTEEL DENIES REPORT AUDIT FOUND POOR FINANCIAL MANAGEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sinosteel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday a local media report that an investigation by China's National Audit Office found the company made risky investments and had large debt because of poor financial management was incorrect, and that it hasn't received such an assessment from any organization or government department. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par METCASH SAYS CONDITIONS REMAIN DIFFICULT; RETAINS EPS GROWTH GUIDANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Metcash Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday trading conditions remain difficult but it maintained its guidance for earnings per share growth in the current fiscal year ending April 30, 2011. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES HIGHER; FINANCIALS UP IN CHINA, TECHS LIFT TOKYO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were higher Thursday as stronger-than-expected U.S. manufacturing data renewed optimism about the global economic recovery. In China, financial stocks were driving the market higher on merger activity, while tech plays and automakers were strong in Japan. (published 0410 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE: WESTERN AUSTRALIA STARTS BROWSE LNG LAND ACQUISITION PROCESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Western Australia state said Thursday that it has commenced a compulsory acquisition process for land planned to accommodate the massive Browse liquefied natural gas project. (published 0230 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RIO TINTO SAYS 4Q IRON ORE PRICE TO FALL 13.3% FROM 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it expects fourth quarter iron ore prices to fall around 13.3% from the third quarter of 2010 to more "sustainable" levels after several price hikes. (published 0508 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CNPC: PETROCHINA COMPLETES WORK ON FIRST LNG TERMINAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has completed construction of its first liquefied natural gas terminal, located in northeastern China's Dalian city, parent company \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday. (published 0544 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA AUG 26-SEP 1 MONSOON RAINS LIKELY 16% ABOVE AVERAGE - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monsoon rains in India were likely 16% above average during the Aug. 26-Sep. 1 period, a senior official with the India Meteorological Department said Thursday. (published 0617 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: WHOLE-MILK POWDER PRICES JUMP 19% IN SEPTEMBER AUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fonterra Co-Operative Group Ltd. said its Internet-based auction for early September saw average whole-milk powder prices jump 18.8% after falling since May, something economists said will increase the chances the dairy giant meets its forecast milk payout for the 2010-2011 production season, pumping billions of dollars into the New Zealand economy. (published 2339 GMT Wednesday) [ 02-09-10 0713GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100902e692000hj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
