\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For August 16\b0\par\par\uc2 1,743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2010\par 09:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: JAPAN GDP GROWTH SLOWS AS CONSUMPTION, EXPORT GAINS SLACKEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economic growth slowed sharply in the second quarter, falling well short of expectations as stagnant consumption and flagging exports weighed on an economy already hobbled by deflation and a soaring yen. (published 0357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA WHOLESALE PRICE INDEX UP 9.97% ON YEAR IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's wholesale inflation decelerated to 9.97% in July from 10.55% in June, the government said Monday. (published 0615 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA LABOR FOCUS ON ECONOMY, HEALTH AT CAMPAIGN LAUNCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Prime Minister Julia Gillard on Monday kicked off her center-left Labor government's official pitch for a second term in office with a focus on the economy and health care, attempting to carve both out as areas where Labor has the upper hand. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAS WON'T \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR AT CURRENT LEVELS-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is comfortable with the local dollar's recent rise and won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  near current levels against the U.S. dollar, a person familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking said Monday. (published 0539 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA JULY IMPORT PRICES DOWN 0.5% ON MONTH; FIRST FALL IN 6 MONTHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's import prices declined in July from the previous month due to a fall in prices of Dubai crude oil and other raw materials, easing inflationary pressures on the economy. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES' MEDIUM-TERM PLAN DOESN'T ENVISAGE BALANCED BUDGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The administration of President Benigno Aquino III isn't looking to balance the budget during its six-year term, but will keep the deficit at a manageable 2% of gross domestic product, the latest medium-term fiscal program of the government showed Monday. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF QUEENSLAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO OFFER A$750M IN RMBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Queensland Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to offer A$750 million in residential mortgage-backed securities, with pricing guidance on the top tranche much improved from earlier this year. (published 2350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: MALAYSIA 2Q GDP LIKELY SLOWED TO 8.4% ON YEAR - POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's trade-driven economy likely moderated in the second quarter from the first, in tandem with slower exports, economists said. (published 0242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: HK MAY-JULY UNEMPLOYMENT RATE LIKELY STEADY AT 4.6% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's unemployment rate likely held steady in the three months ended July 31 as a larger work force, boosted by school-leavers entering the job market, offset the increase in the number of new jobs. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CANADA'S AGRIUM BIDS A$1.50/SHARE FOR AUSTRALIA'S AWB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian agribusiness \f28 \uc2 \f2 AWB Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has received a conditional takeover bid from Canadian fertilizer supplier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agrium Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . pitched at A$1.50 cash a share, valuing the company at A$1.24 billion, even as AWB continues to implement a share-based merger agreement with \f28 \uc2 \f2 GrainCorp Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SIGMA TO SELL PHARMACEUTICAL DIVISION TO ASPEN FOR A$900M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sigma Pharmaceuticals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday announced a surprise deal to sell its pharmaceutical division to South Africa's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aspen Pharmacare Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for A$900 million. (published 0357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: URUGUAY'S UNION AGRICULTURE GROUP MAKES BID FOR NZ FARMING SYSTEMS URUGUAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Uruguay's Union Agriculture Group said Monday it plans to make a full takeover offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 NZ Farming Systems Uruguay Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for NZ$0.60 per share, beating the NZ$0.55 full takeover offer that Singapore-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Olam International\f28 \uc2 \f2  made last month. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COSCO INTERNATIONAL: MAY SELL ENTIRE STAKE IN SINO-OCEAN LAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cosco International Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it may sell its entire 16.85% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sino-Ocean Land Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., as part of the company's divestment of non-core investments. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA ATTACHES CONDITIONS TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 NOVARTIS\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' ACQUISITION OF ALCON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Ministry of Commerce on Friday approved \f28 \uc2 \f2 Novartis AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alcon Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., but attached conditions to the deal in the China market. (published 0451 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: GOODMAN TO ACQUIRE MOORABBIN AIRPORT FOR A$201.5M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commercial property investor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goodman Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it plans to buy Moorabbin airport and business park in Melbourne for A$201.5 million. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: GUNNS TO SELL TAMAR RIDGE; EXPECTS FY10 NET A$28M \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian forestry company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gunns Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it would sell its Tamar Ridge wine unit for A$32.5 million, while also announcing an unaudited net profit for fiscal 2009-10 of A$28.0 million ahead of what one brokerage said could be a messy formal full year result scheduled for Wednesday. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: KB FINANCIAL: OVERSEAS EXPANSION THROUGH M&A POSSIBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 KB Financial Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it may consider mergers or acquisitions to expand in overseas markets such as Singapore and the U.S. as the lender searches for new growth engines beyond the highly competitive domestic market. (published 0129 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAN MIGUEL TAKES CONTROL OF LOCAL FIRM BELL TELECOMMUNICATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 San Miguel Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its wholly-owned unit, Vega Telecom Inc., has taken control of Bell Telecommunication Philippines Inc. through its acquisition of new shares in three local firms that together own 100% of the local telecom services provider. (published 0158 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CLP 1ST-HALF NET PROFIT RISES 83% TO HK$5.92 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CLP Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its first-half net profit rose 83% from year earlier, partly due to higher contributions from its energy business in Australia. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NEWCREST FY NET PROFIT DOUBLES ON SALES, COSTS, PRICE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Newcrest Mining Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that net profit for the year ended June 30 more than doubled to A$556.9 million, from A$248.1 million a year earlier. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: LEND LEASE SWINGS TO A$345.6M FY PROFIT; OPERATING RESULT BEATS GUIDANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lend Lease Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Australia's largest property developer, on Monday swung to a full-year net profit of A$345.6 million, owing to an absence of the near A$1 billion worth of asset writedowns that marred its previous result. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CENTENNIAL COAL NET PROFITS DOWN 28% TO A$51.5M ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , VOLUMES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Centennial Coal Co. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that full-year net profit fell 28% from a year earlier as a strengthening Australian dollar put pressure on export prices. (published 0251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BLUESCOPE STEEL FY NET PROFIT A$126M, RESUMES DIVIDENDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's largest steelmaker \f28 \uc2 \f2 BlueScope Steel Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has returned to profitability with full year earnings of A$126 million and resumed dividend payments but warned that short-term conditions remain tough. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: FREIGHTWAYS FY10 NET DOWN 33% BUT 2H SHOWED IMPROVEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Courier and freight company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Freightways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday said its full-year profit fell 33% but pointed to better performance in the second half as it begins to benefit from New Zealand's gradual economic recovery. (published 0010 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 PYNE GOULD CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  SAYS FY NET PROFIT TO BE 5% HIGHER THAN FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial-services company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pyne Gould Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said its fully year net profit would be around 5% higher than forecast after net operating income strengthened. (published 0320 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UNITECH 1Q CONSOLIDATED NET PROFIT UP 14% AT INR1.80 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Real estate developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Unitech Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . posted a 14% rise in its fiscal first quarter consolidated net profit, helped by higher sales and drop in interest costs. (published 0330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALINTA ENERGY EXPECTS A$465M IMPAIRMENT CHARGE IN 2H10 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Debt-laden power generator Alinta Energy Ltd. said Monday that it expects to book a A$465 million non-cash impairment charge in the second half of last financial year. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AIRPORTS OF THAILAND SWINGS TO 3Q NET LOSS OF THB516.2 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Airports of Thailand PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that it swung to a net loss in the third quarter because of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY LOWER; SOFT JAPAN DATA HIT SENTIMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly lower Monday with weaker-than-expected economic growth from Japan weighing on sentiment across the region, though gains in Chinese shares were helping to stem the losses. (published 0411 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KODECO HALTS 1 RIG'S PRODUCTION AFTER COLLISION -INDONESIAN OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kodeco Energy Ltd. has shut down one of its 14 oil and gas production rigs in a block offshore of East Java after its rig was hit by a container ship last week. (published 0234 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: WOODSIDE STRIKES GAS FOR PLUTO LNG EXPANSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Woodside Petroleum Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that it has found more gas offshore Western Australia state, potentially putting an expansion of its A$13 billion Pluto liquefied natural gas project back on track. (published 0444 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINOPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  ENCOUNTERS RECORD GAS FLOW AT NORTHEAST SICHUAN WELL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Petroleum & Chemical Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has encountered a high flow of natural gas at a well it drilled in Yuanba in gas-rich Sichuan province's northeast, with a record daily output of 1.26 million cubic meters, parent Sinopec Group said in its in-house newsletter Monday. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MISSION TO VISIT VIETNAM TO PITCH NUCLEAR POWER TECHNOLOGY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 16-08-10 0706GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 High-level government and industry officials from Japan plan to visit Vietnam possibly later this month to sell nuclear power plants to the Southeast Asian country for the second phase of its atomic power project, a Japanese government official said Monday. (published 0322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S MACQUARIE TO LAUNCH CROP FUND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A unit of Australia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Macquarie Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday launched a new crop fund aimed at investors looking to increase exposure to the production of grains and oilseeds. (published 0126 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES FORECASTS 2H FARM OUTPUT TO EXPAND 3.8% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine farm production in the second half of the year is expected to expand 3.8% from the same period a year earlier, allowing the sector--which accounts for one-fifth of gross domestic product--to at least "break even" for the year, the Department of Agriculture's chief statistician said Monday. (published 0420 GMT) [ 16-08-10 0706GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0