\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ MAS May  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  If US Dollar Rises Well Above S$1.42 -Source\b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2010\par 05:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 23 May 2010 23:49 EDT *DJ  MAS Comfortable With Singapore Dollar Level Vs US Dlr -Source\par \par \uc2 23 May 2010 23:49 EDT *DJ  Singapore MAS Not Concerned For Now With Euro Fall - Source\par \par \uc2 23 May 2010 23:49 EDT *DJ  MAS Doesn't Expect Strong Euro Rebound In Short Term - Source\par \par \uc2 23 May 2010 23:50 EDT DJ  MAS May \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  If US Dollar Rises Well Above S$1.42 -Source\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is comfortable with the local dollar's moves against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the euro and wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  near current levels, a person familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking said Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore views the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent fall against the U.S. dollar and rise against the euro as part of global trends and won't defend the Singapore dollar unless the U.S. dollar should rise "convincingly" above S$1.4200, the person told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 The greenback was quoted at S$1.4069 at 0345 GMT Monday.\par \par \uc2 "The stronger U.S. dollar is not the result of any fundamental weakness in Singapore, or for that matter, Asia," the person said. "It's because of the debt issues in the euro zone, which hurt the euro. In any case, the dollar is still well within the MAS trading band."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  guides the Singapore dollar within an undisclosed band against a basket of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It uses the exchange rate rather than interest rates because trade dwarfs \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's small domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 Many Asian central banks have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past year to prevent big rises in their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar from crimping their export-reliant economic recoveries. But as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen globally in recent weeks on safe-haven buying due to the European debt crisis, central banks in Indonesia and the Philippines have been selling dollars to support their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say.\par \par \uc2 The MAS aggressively tightened policy in April by raising its trading band for the Singapore dollar in trade-weighted terms and targeting a "modest and gradual appreciation" for the local dollar, changing its previous policy of zero appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar fell as low as S$1.3646 in late April on the policy change but has steadily recovered.\par \par \uc2 The person familiar with the MAS's thinking said the city-state's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "still" not concerned about the falling euro as it hasn't dented Singapore's exports to the European Union.\par \par \uc2 "There is already a slight euro recovery," the person said. "But there are no expectations of sustained euro strength at least in the short-term."\par \par \uc2 The euro fell to an eight-year low of S$1.6971 last week but had rebounded to S$1.7596.\par \par \uc2 The EU is Singapore's biggest trading partner, followed by China and the U.S. In April, Singapore's non-oil domestic exports to the EU rose 21.3% on year to S$1.9 billion, but fell 5.4% on a seasonally adjusted basis from the previous month.\par \par \uc2 -By Singapore Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 23, 2010 23:50 ET (03:50 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100524e65o000az\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
