\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Higher Late On Strong Stocks; MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2010\par 10:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.3718   -0.0046 \par    Overnight rate        0.13%    Unch \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.51%    -1 bp \par    10-year bond yield:   2.76%    Unch \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.18%    Unch \par    10-year swap offer:   2.95%    +4 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   177 bps  +4 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was higher against the U.S. dollar late Wednesday in Asian trade, clocking gains for a second day as a rebound in equities markets buoyed regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar briefly slid below the S$1.3700 mark in late Asian trading but recovered soon after on brief \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to a person familiar with the situation. The MAS may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to cool the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar falls below S$1.3700, he said.\par \par \uc2 An analyst with a local bank said the greenback could find support at the S$1.3670 level if it were to breach the S$1.3700 mark overnight. "We see some risk appetite returning to the markets and the equities markets are driving the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said.\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks gained after U.S. companies such as \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2 . reported higher than expected net income for the first quarter, boosting expectations of a global economic upturn.\par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds were flat in the absence of any local catalysts. Yields at the short end were up in line with that of shorter-maturity U.S. Treasurys, which were up on better investor sentiment following a series of strong earnings reports.\par \par \uc2 -Gaurav Raghuvanshi; Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 154; gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com [ 21-04-10 0805GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100421e64l000p8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
