\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  MAS May  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  If US Dollar Falls 'Well Below' S$1.37 - Source\b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2010\par 07:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Corrected April 15, 2010 01:46 ET (0546 GMT) [ 15-04-10 0534GMT ]\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)-- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was surprised at how much the local dollar rose after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightened policy Wednesday, and the MAS may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps rising, a person familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The MAS "didn't expect such a rise in the Singapore dollar," the person told Dow Jones Newswires. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "expected it to stabilize to around S$1.38 to the U.S. dollar."\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar fell to S$1.3722, near a two-year low, Wednesday after the MAS announced an aggressive tightening--raising the Singapore dollar's trading band and targeting a further "modest and gradual appreciation" of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 0435 GMT the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at S$1.3735.\par \par \uc2 The local dollar is now around the midpoint of the MAS's undisclosed policy band in trade-weighted terms, the person said, adding that if the U.S. dollar "falls well below" S$1.37, "the MAS could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned that if China revalues the yuan, as many expect, that will further boost the Singapore dollar, along with other Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the person said.\par \par \uc2 Forecasting models suggest that even a "slight" yuan revaluation could prompt the U.S. dollar to fall to S$1.33 or lower within a few months, he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tightening, the first in two years, marked the first time it has both raised the trading band and targeted further appreciation of the Singapore dollar. The MAS uses the exchange rate, rather than interest rates, as its main policy tool because Singapore's trade flows dwarf the island's small domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 -By Singapore Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4150; djnews.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com [ 15-04-10 0535GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100415e64f000ck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
