\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, Singapore dollar rise on Greece aid package\b0\par\par\uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2010\par 09:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won rises in both onshore and offshore markets\par \par \uc2 * Singapore dollar rises but capped by c.bank\par \par \uc2 * Thai baht falls amid political turmoil\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, April 12 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Monday as investors bought riskier assets after European Union leaders agreed to a rescue package for Greece, with gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar sparking official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro <EUR=> jumped to 1.3692 from $1.3488 in New York on Friday after investors who had sold it scrambled to cover short positions, weighing broadly on the dollar. [ID:nTOE63B03E]\par \par \uc2 Euro zone finance ministers approved a 30 billion euro ($40.5 billion) aid package of loans for Greece if needed, with 10 billion euros also expected from the International Monetary Fund, a move likely to calm markets in the short term. [ID:nLDE63A0BO]\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won rose in both onshore and offshore markets.\par \par \uc2 One-month offshore dollar/won non-deliverable forwards <KRWNDFOR=> dipped to 1,112 from 1,117.6 late on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "We see heavy selling this morning across dollar/Asians. Risk appetite is back," said a Singapore-based NDF trader.\par \par \uc2 The spot won <KRW=> briefly hit a 19-month high at 1,111.3 per dollar but later pulled back to 1,114 as investors were wary of a dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities.\par \par \uc2 Local importers also bought dollars to settle accounts.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are reluctant to chase it more as the authorities are expected to defend certain levels," said a dealer.\par \par \uc2 Seoul shares <.KS11> fell 0.8 percent with foreign investors sellers of a net 49.2 billion won worth of stocks on the main exchange.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose half of a percent to 1.3838 per U.S. dollar -- the highest in just over four months, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's appreciation much slower," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 -based trader.\par \par \uc2 Ten out of 18 analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a secret trade-weighted band against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to keep its zero appreciation policy at a review on Wednesday. [ID:nSGE62G0F6]\par \par \uc2 Emmanuel Ng, strategist at \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2 , believes Singapore dollar is now around 1.6 percent above the band's central parity compared with the upper ceiling of 2 percent managed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We think there is a 55 percent probability of a reversion to a gradual and modest appreciation," Ng said.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=> lost as much as half of a percent to 32.38 per dollar in line with local stocks <.SETI>, bucking a bullish trend for most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the political turmoil.\par \par \uc2 Thailand's government could propose early elections to defuse a month-long political crisis, a newspaper reported on Monday, although opposition "red shirts" say the time for talks is over after clashes between anti-government protesters and security forces killed 21 people. [ID:nSGE63B008].\par \par \uc2 Traders said expectations that Beijing will allow the yuan to strengthen provided some support for the baht.\par \par \uc2 "Without the former, the baht could fall much deeper today," a Bangkok-based trader said.\par \par \uc2 The baht is still up 3.35 percent so far this year. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0621 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        93.27          93.15       -0.13\par  Sing dlr        1.3887         1.3901       +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr      31.497         31.615       +0.37\par  Korean won     1114.00        1118.20       +0.38\par  Baht             32.26          32.21       -0.15\par  Peso             44.70          44.95       +0.56\par  Rupiah         9000.00        9022.00       +0.24\par  Rupee            44.36          44.28       -0.17\par  Ringgit         3.1980         3.1845       -0.42\par  Yuan            6.8249         6.8239       -0.01\par  Change so far in 2010\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        93.27          92.90       -0.40\par  Sing dlr        1.3887         1.4053       +1.20\par  Taiwan dlr      31.497         32.030       +1.69\par  Korean won     1114.00        1164.50       +4.53\par  Baht             32.26          33.32       +3.29\par  Peso             44.70          46.20       +3.36\par  Rupiah         9000.00        9420.00       +4.67\par  Rupee            44.36          46.54       +4.91\par  Ringgit         3.1980         3.4220       +7.00\par  Yuan            6.8249         6.8270       +0.03\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Vithoon Amorn in BANGKOK and Cheon Jong-woo in SEOUL; Editing by Tomasz Janowski)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|Tab