\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso, Singapore dollar gain, yuan NDFs edge up\b0\par\par\uc2 893 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Peso gains, buoyed by offshore/onshore arbitrage\par \par \uc2  * Yuan NDFs inch up as China tries to cool \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  spat\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar capped by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  By Kevin Yao\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , March 19 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso gained on Friday as investors tried to profit from a spread between offshore and onshore forwards, while suspected official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.\par \par \uc2  Several Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Malaysian ringgit and Singapore dollar, are on track for their sixth straight week of gains, in line with Asian stocks and supported by growing optimism about a sustained economic recovery in the region.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro stabilised but remained under pressure after Greece said it could not achieve promised deficit cuts if its borrowing costs remain so high. [ID:nTOE62I04M]\par \par \uc2  PESO\par \par \uc2  The peso <PHP=> gained a third of a percent to 45.54 per dollar, matching a 19-month high hit on Wednesday, as investors continued to profit from a gap in onshore/offshore forwards.\par \par \uc2  "A lot of banks and some corporate accounts have been taking advantage of the arbitrage between the onshore and offshore markets, that's why dollar/peso has been trading lower despite the weakness in the euro overnight," said a dealer in Manila.\par \par \uc2  Investors bought dollar/peso offshore and reversed the trade onshore in arbitrage trade, which translated into fund inflows.\par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/peso NDFs <PHP1MNDFOR=> fell to 45.69 from 45.73 late on Thursday while 1-month onshore forwards <PHP1M=> eased to 45.73 from 45.741.\par \par \uc2  The spread between one-month onshore/NDFs has narrowed to 40 points from around 110 points a week earlier.\par \par \uc2  YUAN\par \par \uc2  The yuan edged up NDFs in tenors up to one year after declines earlier this week, as Commerce Ministry official He Ning says on Friday that channels of communication are open for discussing trade issues, including yuan. [ID:nBJB003743].\par \par \uc2  But traders believe yuan NDFs are unlikely to form a major uptrend before a critical semi-annual U.S. Treasury report due April 15.\par \par \uc2  "Any bets now either way would involve lots of risk, with stakes too high for the reward. NDFs may move sideways in coming weeks," said an analyst at U.S bank in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2  One-year dollar/yuan NDFs eased to 6.6598 from Thursday's close of 6.6640, implying a 2.5 percent yuan rise from day's mid-point, up fractionally from Thursday.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose a fifth of a percent to 1.3915 per U.S. dollar on growing optimism about the economy, but traders said the unit was contained by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "The only real big (dollar) buyer in the market is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and they will probably continue till the next policy meeting in April," said trader in Singapore.\par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar has gained just 0.8 percent so far this year, the second-worst performer in Asia after the Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS>, which is virtually pegged to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2  Most Analysts expect Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its neutral \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in the April meeting despite signs of economic recovery is gaining steam.\par \par \uc2  RINGGIT\par \par \uc2  The ringgit <MYR=> gained a fifth of a percent to 3.297 per dollar, extending its gains so far this year to 3.8 percent and making it the top performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  has raised its end-2010 forecast on the ringgit to 3.13 per dollar from 3.20, citing Malaysia's improving balance of payments and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy tightening.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised investors by raising interest rates earlier this month.\par \par \uc2  "We also recognise that the ringgit has a potential 'bonus fundamental', given that it is perceived to benefit the most from a yuan revaluation scenario in Asia ex-Japan," analysts at the bank said in a note.\par \par \uc2  Investors should profit from further gains in ringgit via NDFs, call spread and risk-reversals, they suggested.  Change on the day at 0654 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        90.43          90.37       -0.07\par  Sing dlr        1.3943         1.3964       +0.15\par  Taiwan dlr      31.732         31.825       +0.29\par  Korean won     1132.50        1133.70       +0.11\par  Baht             32.29          32.30       +0.03\par  Peso             45.54          45.69       +0.33\par  Rupiah         9100.00        9120.00       +0.22\par  Rupee            45.46          45.45       -0.04\par  Ringgit         3.2970         3.3050       +0.24\par  Yuan            6.8260         6.8261       +0.00\par  Change so far in 2010\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        90.43          92.90       +2.73\par  Sing d