\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Rises Late On Broad Slide In U.S. Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2009\par 08:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.3796   -0.0029 \par    Overnight rate        0.375%   -0.255 \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.58%    -2 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.46%    +1 bp \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.41%    unchanged \par    10-year swap offer:   2.88%    -1 bp \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   147 bps  -1 bp \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar ended the Asian session stronger Thursday as its U.S. counterpart continued to weaken against most \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 The key for the U.S. dollar's weakness was the euro rising above the psychologically significant US$1.51 level Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The fall in the greenback against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was checked in part by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the U.S. dollar, two persons familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 One person said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around S$1.3797 and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue supporting the greenback if needed.\par \par \uc2 However, one trader said with the U.S. dollar having broken down through key levels on a trade-weighted basis, there is still plenty of scope for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drop to the S$1.3700 level.\par \par \uc2 He said while Asian equities were slightly weaker Thursday, risk appetite is "neutral."\par \par \uc2 "There's a bit of a correction in the stock markets today but I think the trend is for more Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation near-term," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds were stronger at the short end, supported by the modest downturn in regional equities.\par \par \uc2 -By Sam Holmes, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4157; samuel.holmes@dowjones.com [ 26-11-09 0737GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091126e5bq000j0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
