\par\par \b \uc2 Reuters Southeast Asia News Highlights 0900 GMT Nov 19\b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2009\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE - Singapore sees a return to modest growth and higher inflation next year, which may spur the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tighten policy in April by allowing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gradually strengthen.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  joined other policymakers around Asia in saying it was watching property prices and lifted its 2010 inflation forecast to between 2.5 and 3.5 percent on Thursday, as a flood of foreign investment raises asset bubble worries. [ID:nSP485086]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is studying a possible limit on foreign ownership of one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt (SBI), the shortest SBI tenor, as an option to control hot money flows, a source with knowledge of the study said.\par \par \uc2 The source said such a move would be aimed at getting foreign investors to shift to longer maturities. [ID:nJAK492570]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK - A diplomatic row between Cambodia and Thailand has moved into the skies after Phnom Penh took control of a Thai-operated air traffic control company at the centre of spying allegations.\par \par \uc2 The Cambodian government has appointed a senior Civil Aviation official as temporary caretaker for Cambodia Air Traffic Services (CATS), a wholly owned unit of Thailand's \uc2 Samart Corporation\uc2  Pcl, Samart said on Thursday. [ID:nBKK426725]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK - Thailand's economy is expected to grow 3.5 percent next year after returning to positive annual growth in the final quarter of 2009, Prime Minister Abhisit Vejjajiva said. "We are confident that the economy will turn positive in the final quarter.\par \par \uc2 It is expected to grow 3.5 percent next year, but this could be revised in the future," he told a seminar. [ID:nBKK487811]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the weakening rupiah on persistent jitters over possible steps to curb foreign flows, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "BI (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) kept selling dollar/rupiah from 9,460," said a Jakarta-based trader. [ID:nSP501547]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR - Shares in Malaysia's top mobile phone operator \uc2 Maxis Bhd\uc2  have little upside due to the sector's steep valuations and sluggish growth prospects after its $3.3 billion initial public offering made a strong market debut.\par \par \uc2 Maxis joins Chinese developer \uc2 Longfor Properties Co\uc2  in delivering impressive openings on Thursday as Asia dominates as the world's top region for companies tapping markets for funds this year. [ID:nKLR425244] (Compiled by Carl Bagh)\par \par \uc2 SOUTHEAST ASIA-HIGHLIGHTS 0900 GMT|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|O|OIL|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|G|SI|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNP|DNP|PGE|PCM|PEN|SXNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091119e5bj000kx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
