\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,000 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2009\par 06:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP:SINGAPORE OCTOBER NON-OIL EXPORTS FELL 6.1% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's key exports contracted at a sharper than anticipated rate in October, government data showed Tuesday. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN DEPUTY PM: EXTRA BUDGET NOT CAPPED AT Y2.7 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Deputy Prime Minister Naoto Kan backpedaled Tuesday from a figure of Y2.7 trillion for the government's upcoming extra budget, saying he has decided not to set an upper limit for now. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =JAPAN BANK MINISTER URGES MORE BOJ EFFORTS TO SUPPORT GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's outspoken bank minister Shizuka Kamei on Tuesday criticized the Bank of Japan for not doing enough to rejuvenate growth, calling on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to "play a more active role" in supporting the still-fragile economy. (published 0412 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: RBA MINUTES: MORE HIKES NEEDED, PACE AN OPEN QUESTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Tuesday flagged further gradual increases in interest rates but said it is unsure how quickly it will make the policy adjustments. (published 0131 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF KOREA:TO RUN MONETARY POLICY IN LINE WITH GLOBAL TREND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will operate its monetary policy in line with the global trend, a Bank of Korea official said Tuesday. (published 0403 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WORLD BANK: CHINA LIKELY TO GROW 8%-10% IN COMING YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese economy is expected to grow between 8% and 10% in coming years on "good" infrastructure, World Bank Chief Economist Justin Yifu Lin said Tuesday. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA'S KEXIM PLANS $8 BLN GLOBAL BOND ISSUE NEXT YEAR-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Export-Import Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to offer around $8 billion in global bonds next year, a senior official at the state-run bank said Tuesday. (published 0344 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: SINOCHEM TO SELL $500 MLN OF US DOLLAR BONDS - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China National Chemicals Import & Export Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Sinochem Corp., plans to sell $500 million worth of dollar-denominated bonds on the domestic interbank market in late November to finance its overseas expansion, a person familiar with the situation said Tuesday. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TEMASEK RAISES $500 MLN IN SECOND GLOBAL BOND SALE THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Temasek Holdings Pte Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the Singapore government-owned investment company, has returned to the international bond market for the second time this year to raise $500 million via a 30-year bond. (published 0024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OBAMA: SMALL MEETING TALKS WITH CHINA SO FAR CONSTRUCTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In remarks carried live on state television, Obama, sitting across a meeting table from Chinese President Hu Jintao, said he looks forward to expanded discussions with the Chinese government, and the American people want stronger relations with the people of China. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJ CEO COUNCIL: CEOS REMAIN HESITANT TO HIRE NEW WORKERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. corporations remain hesitant to give the gift of a new job this holiday season, except for a select few. (published 0206 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FUJII: WANT TO KEEP FISCAL 2010 JGB ISSUANCE BELOW Y44T \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Hirohisa Fujii on Tuesday expressed his desire to keep planned government debt sales below Y44 trillion in the next fiscal year starting in April, saying excessive bond issuance would be troubling. (published 0013 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE MAS SUPPORTED U.S. DOLLAR MONDAY, TUESDAY -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Monday and Tuesday to slow the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise against the U.S. dollar, a person familiar with the situation said. (published 0128 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: ANOTHER ECONOMIC STIMULUS COULD COME NEXT YR - BOFA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts believe another economic stimulus package could come next year if more jobs are not created. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF: TIME TO MOVE FORWARD ON GLOBAL FINANCIAL SYSTEM REFORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Now is the right time to try to move forward on the reform of international financial system, the head of the International Monetary Fund said Tuesday. (published 0251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OECD CHIEF: EXPECT SOUTH KOREA'S GROWTH IN 2010 TO BE OVER 4% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economic growth is likely to be flat or slightly positive in 2009, and is expected to be over 4% next year, OECD Secretary-General Angel Gurria said Tuesday. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA MOF TO SELL CNY30 BLN NONTRADABLE BONDS NOV. 20-DEC. 6 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it will issue CNY30 billion worth of nontradable bonds to individual investors from Nov. 20 to Dec. 6. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FED'S KOHN SAYS BEWARE OF FALSE SIGNS OF ASSET BUBBLES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Vice Chairman Donald Kohn said Monday that Fed policy works best when focused on promoting long-term financial stability, not taking actions to correct specific financial problems. (published 0043 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: KOHN: FED NOT READY TO HIKE RATES TO PRICK BUBBLES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve should not try to prick what some see as a new bubble forming in financial markets, a Fed official said Monday, even though he admitted that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's reluctance to target asset prices may have contributed to the financial crisis. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:BOE SENTANCE: NO DECISION THAT NO MORE EASING NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of England hasn't yet made the judgment that its stimulus measures have gone far enough, but short-term economic news has generally been "very positive," Monetary Policy Committee member Andrew Sentance said Monday. (published 2331 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DOLLAR/YEN OPTIONS UP ON VIEWS DOLLAR MAY DROP TO Y87 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen options rose in Tokyo Tuesday due to increased demand for hedges, with investors seeing a weaker dollar and stronger yen due to the Federal Reserve's dovish stance and potential spillover from political pressure on the yuan. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: BERNANKE GIVES GEITHNER A HAND ON DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After Ben Bernanke let it be known Monday that the Federal Reserve is focused on a strong dollar, the euro dived almost a full cent against the greenback. (published 2113 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 17-11-09 0504GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091117e5bh000az\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
