\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht rebounds,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk caps  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  dlr\b0\par\par\uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2009\par 07:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Baht rebounds from 2-week low in line with local stocks\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar firms, but capped by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk\par \par \uc2 * Ringgit falls from 14-month high as investors book profits\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 16 (Reuters) - The Thai baht rebounded on Friday in step with local stocks after two days of losses sparked by concerns over the health of the country's king, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's gains were limited by talk of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=> stayed under broad pressure as investors cut some of their long positions, while sterling <GBP=D4> approached its highest level in three weeks following upbeat \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments. [IDnT126523]\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=> rebounded to 33.37 per dollar from its two-week low of 33.61 hit on Thursday, in line with a bounce back in stocks after a palace official said the king's health was improving.\par \par \uc2 The palace official said on Thursday that the 81-year-old king was on the mend but he would still need protracted physical therapy. He has been in hospital for nearly a month and is recovering from pneumonia.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said on Friday that Thailand has no need to adopt special measures to support the stock market after its biggest fall in a year, and added that he expected the country's economic fundamentals to remain sound. [ID:nBKT003111]\par \par \uc2 "The baht would probably hover around this level with the focus on the stock market. If stocks face a renewed broad sell-off, baht will follow," said a trader.\par \par \uc2 Other dealers said many investors may protectively close out \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions ahead of the weekend.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> drifted towards 1.388 per U.S. dollar, but its upside was contained by talk of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We see good two way interest with market rumours the authority is supporting the U.S. dollar at 1.3880," said a trader.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, traders suspected official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rose to 1.3856, its highest since August 2008.\par \par \uc2 Singapore dollar has gained 4 percent since early Sept. as part of an Asia-wide rally against the beleaguered U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Earlier this week, Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its zero appreciation stance on hold and sounded wary on the country's economic outlook.\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The ringgit <MYR=> eased to 3.37 per dollar, down 0.4 percent from Thursday, when it hit a 14-month high.\par \par \uc2 "Obviously the market is very short dollars, people are squaring up as we go into weekend," said a trader.\par \par \uc2 The ringgit is set to gain 0.7 percent this week, slowing from its 2 percent jump in the previous week -- the sharpest rally this year. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0543 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        90.91          90.55       -0.40\par  Sing dlr        1.3914         1.3900   