\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected as dollar suffers\b0\par\par\uc2 950 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2009\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2  * Firmer baht, peso prompt central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Traders spot U.S. dollar buying to cap \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar\par \par \uc2  * Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains seen intact despite official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  By Kevin Yao\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 13 (Reuters) - Renewed weakness in the U.S. dollar on Tuesday pushed the Thai baht and Philippine peso towards last week's multi-month highs, triggering fresh official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb their strength.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rose but its gains were also limited by suspected official dollar-buying, a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its zero appreciation policy intact and sounded wary on the economic outlook. [ID:nSP502821]\par \par \uc2  Although central banks are tapping on the brakes, analysts expect the rally in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar to continue as foreign investors flock to regional stock and bond markets on a view the economies will recover from the global downturn faster than the rest of the world.\par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself cannot stop this Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally," said Suresh Ramanathan, strategist at CIMB Investment Bank.\par \par \uc2  "If policy makers need to get out of this directional play in Asia ex-Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the need is to spell out clearly a time frame for exit strategies, this at least provides the market with a framework in gauging how far Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  can strengthen."\par \par \uc2  The dollar stayed weak against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <.DXY> on Tuesday after falling overnight. Investors are shifting into higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a belief that U.S. corporate earnings will exceed expectations boosts risk appetite. [ID:nT311772]\par \par \uc2  India's markets were shut for holiday.\par \par \uc2  BAHT\par \par \uc2  The Thai baht <THB=> firmed in early trade on Tuesday and was expected to move in a narrow range of 33.25-33.40, although dealers spotted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  providing support for the dollar.\par \par \uc2  "The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  was in the market to support dollar/baht at 33.30," said a Bangkok-based trader.\par \par \uc2  It reached an intraday peak of 33.25, moving close to a 14-month high struck last week of 33.22\par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2  The peso <PHP=> rose briefly to 46.49 per dollar, up 0.3 percent from Monday's close, edging back towards last week's 2009 high of 46.45.\par \par \uc2  But it soon pulled back to 46.50 as traders spotted official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the day's high.\par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at 46.50," said a Manila-based trader, adding the such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not aggressive.\par \par \uc2  The peso has gained only 2 percent against the dollar so far this year, trailing the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=>, which has rallied nearly 17 percent, and the South Korean won's 8 percent gain <KRW=>.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar <SGD=> gained a quarter of percent to 1.3962 per U.S. dollar but it was capped by suspected U.S. dollar-buying by local banks on the behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some traders said.\par \par \uc2  "Agent names have been on the bid (for USD) since yesterday and they are still bidding, while the market prefers to sell U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar," said a trader.\par \par \uc2  Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its zero appreciation policy on Monday was cautious about the economic outlook. [ID:nSP502821]\par \par \uc2  "We continue to expect the Singapore dollar to trade close to the top of the authority's target band and believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will manage the balance of payments surplus via \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot and forward \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, with a view towards keeping short-term interest rates low and stable," analysts at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The analysts forecast the Singapore dollar would rise to 1.38 to the U.S. dollar by the end of this year and rise further to 1.34 by the end of 2010.\par \par \uc2  YUAN\par \par \uc2  The Chinese yuan was little changed to 6.8260 per dollar, even though many analysts expect Chinese policy makers to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to resume its steady appreciation once the country's exports rise again.\par \par \uc2  A banking regulator was quoted on Tuesday by Chinese media as calling for Beijing to let the yuan rise smartly against the dollar if the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakens, even though Chinese exports are already under pressure. [ID:nPEK313727]\par \par \uc2 China has in effect re-pegged the yuan around 6.83 per dollar since the financial crisis intensified in the middle of 2008 to help its export industries and to cement financial stability.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par