\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Singapore dlr eases on profit-taking after MAS policy\b0\par\par\uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2009\par 02:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2  * Singapore dollar falls in line with regional peers\par \par \uc2  * MAS caution on economy, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk hurt sentiment\par \par \uc2  * Further gains in store on U.S. dollar's expected weakness  (Adds fresh comments)\par \par \uc2  By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Oct 12 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar eased on Monday as investors took profits from its recent gains after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stuck to a neutral bias in its policy review but appeared wary about prospects for exports and global growth.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar fell in tandem with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a broadly firmer U.S. dollar, with sentiment overshadowed by talk of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  In an expected move, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), which steers monetary policy by managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nominal effective exchange rate (NEER) within a undisclosed band, kept its zero appreciation policy unchanged.\par \par \uc2  The move came as the economy expanded 0.8 percent in the third quarter of 2009 from a year earlier, returning to growth after three quarters of annual contraction.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> fell as far as 1.4010 per U.S. dollar, down nearly 0.4 percent from Friday's close and compared to levels of 1.3950 just before the policy announcement.\par \par \uc2  "U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar is higher on profit taking and also on comments from MAS that the economy is not seen sustaining strong third-quarter expansion and that export demand has yet to recover fully for a place that lives and dies on exports," said a trader.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in offshore trading late on Friday by buying U.S. dollars at 1.3910-1.3920 to curb the rise in the local unit, which has gained 10 percent against the U.S. dollar since early March, traders said.\par \par \uc2  Emmanuel Ng, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2 , said he expected the pro-growth \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit further gains in the Singapore dollar, which is seen near its the upper end of its trade-weighted band.\par \par \uc2  "In the next 24-48 hours however, a slightly firmer broad U.S. dollar tone may however take the pressure off the authorities in terms of keeping the NEER in check," he said.\par \par \uc2  FURTHER GAINS IN STORE\par \par \uc2  The MAS said there could be some upward inflation pressures from higher oil and food prices, though underlying domestic cost pressures will be contained. [IDnSP505033]\par \par \uc2  "Inflation is well under control. Thus there is no pressing need for Singapore to tighten policy now," said David Cohen, economist at Action Economics in Singapore.\par \par \uc2  "Singapore is keeping its policy neutral against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so this represents continued appreciation against the U.S. dollar, which has been weakening against the rest of the world," he said.\par \par \uc2  The MAS targets Singapore dollar's relative value compared with a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of trading partners, instead of setting interest rates.\par \par \uc2  In April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered the centre of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to help stimulate the economy, which leapt out its worst ever recession in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2  To read more on the policy statement and GDP data for the third quarter, click on [SG-MCE-LEN-RTRS]  (Editing by Kim Coghill)    \par \par \uc2 MARKETS/SINGAPORE-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091012e5ac0000s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
