\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Higher Late; MAS Steps In To Defend US Dlr\b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2009\par 09:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.4027   -0.0074 \par    Overnight rate        0.50%    +31 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.58%    -1 bp \par    10-year bond yield:   2.41%    +2 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.43%    -4 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   2.82%    +2 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:  139 bps   +6 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose to a 13-month high against the U.S. dollar in late Asian trade Tuesday as monetary tightening steps taken by Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prompted demand for high-yielding assets across Asia.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The fall in the U.S. dollar, which was bid as low as S$1.3997, prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the greenback. It was the greenback's lowest level since late August last year.\par \par \uc2 "There's a lot of pressure on the (U.S.) dollar across Asia," a person familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires. "MAS will continue to try to smoothen the fall."\par \par \uc2 A stronger Singapore dollar could hurt the country's exporters and stunt growth at a time when the economy is showing signs of recovering from a devastating fall in external demand in late 2008.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  tightened policy by increasing its cash rate target by a quarter of a percentage point to 3.25%, citing a need to remove expansionary policy. The move prompted investors to bet on high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also, strong Asian equities due to an overnight rally on the Wall Street also pushed demand for local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The global recovery story remains intact...and the Asian growth story remains strong and the economy will continue to see fund inflows," a trader with a foreign bank said.\par \par \uc2 Another trader with a local bank said that investors will now look at the MAS' policy due next week, although many expect that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stand pat.\par \par \uc2 "Even as I don't expect them to tighten policy, the MAS statement could be hawkish, pointing to possible tightening going forward," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 Singapore uses the exchange rate as its policy tool to support growth and tame inflation as the city-state's economy is mostly driven by exports.\par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, prices were mostly flat in line with overnight moves in U.S. Treasurys.\par \par \uc2 "We could see some selling in the long-end bonds as some choose to move into the equity market," said a trader with a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 -By P.R. Venkat, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 152; venkat.pr@dowjones.com [ 06-10-09 0758GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091006e5a6000bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
