\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  dlr up, won strength sparks  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2009\par 08:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 22 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rose on Tuesday against a broadly weaker U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but its gains were capped by fears of possible official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the South Korean won's strength prompted authorities to buy dollars.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar eased broadly after rallying on Monday when traders took profits on short dollar positions ahead of key events such as a Federal Reserve policy meeting and a Group of 20 summit. [ID:nT239170] Markets in Japan, Malaysia and Indonesia were shut for a holiday.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose 0.3 percent to 1.4145 per U.S. dollar, but it failed to advance further as investors weighed the prospect of a possible official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be reaching the upper end of its secret band.\par \par \uc2 "The Singapore dollar is so far stuck in a tight range," said a Singapore-based trader. "It seems that the Singapore dollar is close to the stronger end of the band, so I reckon support for U.S. dollar will be at 1.4140-50."\par \par \uc2 The Singagpore dollar has jumped 10 percent since early March, buoyed by optimism about the global economy.\par \par \uc2 Some investors were keen to sell the Singapore dollar against the euro and the Australian dollar, traders said.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> rose a fifth of a percent to 1,201.75 per dollar as foreigners bought local stocks, but the authorities moved quickly to curb its strength by buying dollars, traders said. [ID:nSEO240493]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  more frequently as the won has crept closer towards the crucial 1,200-per-dollar level after hitting an 11-month high on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, three-month implied volatilities in the won <KRW3MO=> slipped further to 12.85 percent, its lowest since August 2008 -- just before a spike in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatilities caused by the collapse of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Volatilities are softer as nobody wants to buy options," said a Singapore-based trader. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at  0539 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        91.70          92.00       +0.33\par  Sing dlr        1.4142         1.4185       +0.30\par  Taiwan dlr      32.368         32.419       +0.16\par  Korean won     1202.65        1204.40       +0.15\par  Baht             33.67          33.70       +0.09\par  Peso             47.62          47.70       +0.17\par  Rupee            48.18          48.13       -0.10\par  Yuan            6.8280         6.8289       +0.01\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        91.70          90.60       -1.20\par  Sing dlr        1.4142         1.4340       +1.40\par  Taiwan dlr      32.368         32.860       +1.52\par  Korean won     1202.65        1259.50       +4.73\par  Baht             33.67          34.80       +3.36\par  Peso             47.62          47.52       -0.21\par  Rupiah         9690.00       11000.00      +13.52\par  Rupee           