\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2009\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: BOJ LEAVES OVERNIGHT CALL RATE UNCH, UPS ECON VIEW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's policy board voted Thursday to keep interest rates unchanged at ultra-low levels, but upgraded its assessment of the domestic economy for the first time since July. (published 0451 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:JAPAN MOF:BIG CO SENTIMENT TURNS POSITIVE IN JUL-SEPT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sentiment among large Japanese firms improved in the July-September quarter from the previous three months as they see the economy as having bottomed out, but they still intend to cut spending as they retain a cautious economic outlook. (published 0239 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA GOVT ECONOMIST: 3Q GDP LIKELY UP 9% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economy is likely to grow 9% in the third quarter compared with the year-earlier period, and to accelerate further to double-digit growth in the fourth quarter, an economist affiliated with the country's economic planning agency said Thursday. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN: STIMULUS MUST BE KEPT IN PLACE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Treasurer Wayne Swan Thursday renewed calls for economic stimulus to remain in place, saying significant threats remain to the global economy and warning that unemployment is set to rise. (published 2231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN: ECONOMIC STIMULUS SUPPORTING JOBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Treasurer, Wayne Swan, said Thursday that a timely government economic stimulus package is supporting employment, business and confidence in the economy. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA FIN MIN:TO "FINE TUNE" WON'S STRENGTH IN CASE OF ABNORMALITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to slow the won's appreciation if sentiment is heavily biased to one side, Minister of Strategy and Finance Yoon Jeung-hyun said Thursday. (published 0540 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FIN MIN: ECON LIKELY TO BE FLAT AFTER MODEST RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean economy will likely stagnate once it recovers modestly from the current downturn, Minister of Strategy and Finance Yoon Jeung-hyun said Thursday. (published 0505 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO SUPPORT US DLR AT S$1.4107-SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to support the U.S. dollar at S$1.4107, a person familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par *US DOLLAR TRADED AT S$1.4095 VS S$1.4153 IN ASIA LATE WED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: SINGAPORE AUG EXPORTS DN 7.1% ON YR;SLOWLY RECOVERING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pace of the contraction in Singapore's key exports data continued to moderate in August, indicating the city-state's economy remains on a path of gradual recovery. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN RBA SOLD A$576M IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MKT IN AUG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  sold a net A$576 million in the spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in August, figures issued by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday show. (published 0133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN MERCHANDISE IMPORTS DOWN ADJ 4.0% IN AUG VS JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian merchandise imports fell 4.0% to A$16.19 billion in August from A$16.84 million in July in seasonally adjusted terms, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said Thursday. (published 0134 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA INDUSTRIAL TRENDS INDEX UP 9.8 PTS 3Q VS 2Q - SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's manufacturing and broader industrial pulse showed signs of accelerating in the third quarter, according to a survey released Thursday by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and the Australian Chamber of Commerce and Industry. (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA SHOULD MULL STEPS TO CONTROL SHORT-TERM LIQUIDITY -KDI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean authorities should take preemptive measures to control short-term liquidity to prevent a potential bubble in asset prices from forming due to stimulus measures introduced in the past year, a state-run think tank said Thursday. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NZ AUGUST MANUFACTURING PMI PULLS BACK SLIGHTLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's manufacturing activity weakened slightly, August data released Thursday showed, underscoring the fragile nature of the economic recovery. (published 2321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA AUGUST DEPARTMENT STORE SALES RISE MOST IN 7 MONTHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sales at South Korea's top department stores rose for a sixth consecutive month in August from a year earlier, suggesting that consumption is gradually recovering, the Ministry of Knowledge Economy said Thursday. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES' BALANCE OF PAYMENTS SURPLUS $53M IN AUG - DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines had a balance of payments surplus of $53 million in August, reversing a $54-million deficit in the same month last year, data issued Thursday by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MALAYSIA AUTO GRP: AUGUST NEW VEHICLE SALES +2.8% AT 48,538 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sales of new motor vehicles in Malaysia, Southeast Asia's biggest passenger car market, rose 2.8% on year in August, the Malaysian Automotive Association said Thursday. (published 0403 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TAIWAN CABINET APPROVES RETRACTING CTRL GOVT, SPECIAL BUDGETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's Cabinet approved Thursday the retraction of the central government's 2010 budget, a special budget for economic stimulus spending and a special budget for typhoon reconstruction work due to the recent Cabinet reshuffle. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TAIWAN PM MULLS EXTENDING FULL DEPOSIT INSUR BY 1 YR - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan Premier Wu Den-yih is considering extending the government's full insurance of bank deposits by a year to the end of 2010, the Commercial Times reported Thursday, citing Kuomintang legislator Tsai Cheng-Yuan. (published 0255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: COUNTRY GARDEN SELLS ADDITIONAL US$75M OF 2014 BOND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese property developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Country Garden Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it has sold an additional US$75 million of its existing 2014 global bond to help fund new projects and repay bank loans. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CHINA DEVELOPMENT BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SELL UP TO CNY40B SUB BONDS NEXT WK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Development Bank Corp. said Thursday it plans to sell up to CNY40 billion worth of subordinated bonds on the interbank market next week. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF: TURKEY FISCAL PLAN APPROPRIATE, MUST CONTROL SPENDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund welcomed Turkey's plan Wednesday to reduce its budget deficit, and urged the government to take measures to control spending. (published 0225 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: US DOLLAR DROUGHT CAUSES SOME ANGST IN ASIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian central bankers have been busy little bees in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in recent days, and are likely to remain active as they seek to put a lid on their domestic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(9/17) HEARD ON THE ST: CARRY TRADERS GO EXPLORING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A stable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , resurgent economy and elevated interest rates. Such a target for carry traders exists in familiar territory: Australia. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS:DLR/YEN OPTIONS EDGE DOWN; MAY RISE AGAIN SOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options edged down in Asia Thursday as the underlying exchange rate remained firm, causing some investors to sell protection against the dollar's downside. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FED WATCH: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FACES FEW WORRIES ON FUTURE INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The end of the deflation threat doesn't mean higher inflation lurks around the corner. (published 2010 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ(9/17) DIVINING THE NEXT MOVES BY BERNANKE'S FED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A book published 25 years ago about the Federal Reserve had a wonderful title: "An Intentional Mystery." It was an apt description of an institution that styled itself on ancient oracles whose influence derived from their mystique. (published 0042 GMT) [ 17-09-09 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090917e59h0005p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
