\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Higher Late On Risk Appetite; Bonds Mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2009\par 09:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD              1.4153   -0.0076 \par    Overnight rate        0.19%    Unchanged \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.53%   +2 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.37%    Unchanged \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.52%   +4 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   2.85%   -1 bp \par    2-10-yr swap curve:  133 bps  -5 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was higher in Asian trade late Wednesday, buoyed by stronger risk appetite.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar ground lower against the euro and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the session wore on, continuing to weaken after U.S. stocks gained overnight and Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said the U.S. recession is "very likely over." A firmer start on European bourses also likely further undercut the greenback.\par \par \uc2 But a trader with a local bank said the market remains cautious about pushing the Singapore dollar much higher due to fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.\par \par \uc2 "Market caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains on the radar," OCBC said in a report, while noting the local dollar's strength in nominal effective exchange-rate terms.\par \par \uc2 The MAS, which uses the Singapore dollar as its chief policy tool by managing it in an undisclosed band, has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in recent months to slow the pace of appreciation. Analysts say Asian central banks will be wary of letting their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate too much due to worries about export competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Local government bonds were mixed, with relatively little movement as the market awaits the announcement of the size of the five-year government bond auction due later this month.\par \par \uc2 -By Se Young Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 6415 4155; vincent.lee@dowjones.com [ 16-09-09 0751GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090916e59g000a2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
