\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Higher Late, But  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Linger\b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2009\par 10:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.4216   -0.0020 \par    Overnight rate        0.19%    -6 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.50%    -1 bp \par    10-year bond yield:   2.45%    Unchanged \par    Two-year swap offer:  1.47%    -7 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   2.89%    -2 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:  142 bps   +5 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was trading higher against the U.S. dollar in late Asian trade Friday, as investors' risk appetite for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained firm.\f28 \par \par \uc2 But traders continue to warn that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the local unit rises at a faster-than-expected pace.\par \par \uc2 Traders said that Friday's gains in the Singapore dollar were also driven by the overnight rise in the euro as the local unit's movement mirrored that of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Risk aversion seems to have taken a back seat and investors are getting more optimistic about the global economy," said a trader with a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 Another trader at a local bank, however, warned that the local unit might still hold below the psychological S$1.4200 against the U.S. dollar as many fear that the MAS may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the greenback.\par \par \uc2 "Although, risk appetite has been better, the market continues to be cautious on fears that MAS might come in if the U.S. dollar falls at a faster pace," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 The MAS uses the exchange rate as its policy tool to support growth and maintain price stability in the export-dependent economy. It targets an undisclosed trading band for the Singapore dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the local government bond market, prices barely moved as most of the investors were on the sidelines ahead of the last trading day of the week.\par \par \uc2 "There was some buying in the short end, but it wasn't much as some banks were just looking to position themselves," said another trader with a foreign bank.\par \par \uc2 -By P.R. Venkat, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 152; venkat.pr@dowjones.com [ 11-09-09 0802GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090911e59b000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
