 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to support the U.S. dollar if it falls convincingly below S$1.4200, a person familiar with the situation said Wednesday. (published 0206 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ SUDA: ROLE OF CORP FUNDING AID STEPS RECEDING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan board member Miyako Suda said Wednesday that the role of special programs to aid firms fundraising has been receding recently as corporate financial conditions are improving. (published 0227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GENTING SINGAPORE PLANNING US$1B RIGHTS ISSUE - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Genting Singapore PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is planning to raise about US$1 billion in a rights issue, two people familiar with the situation said Wednesday. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par QANTAS CONSIDERS AIR PACIFIC SALE FOR \f28 \uc2 \f2 VIRGIN BLUE\f28 \uc2 \f2  FIJI BLOCK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is seeking to sell its stake in Fiji's national carrier Air Pacific as part of its move to block the planned expansion on the route to the island nation of its main domestic rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 Virgin Blue Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . . (published 0216 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HANWHA GROUP: NOT INTERESTED IN BUYING DAEWOO ENGINEERING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hanwha Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  Wednesday said that it is not interested in buying \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daewoo Engineering & Construction Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., in response to a media report that it was pursuing the acquisition. (published 0159 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: COMMITTEE TO URGE NO OPEC QUOTAS CHANGE-KUWAIT OIL MIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A three-nation OPEC committee Tuesday agreed to recommend, as expected, that the oil producers' group should leave its existing output quotas unchanged but improve its compliance levels, Kuwaiti oil minister Sheikh Ahmad Abdullah al-Sabah said. (published 2220 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ(9/9) INDONESIA CRACKS OPEN POWER SECTOR FOR INVESTORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAKARTA, Indonesia -- Indonesia's parliament moved to open the state-dominated power sector to more private investment, a potential step toward resolving electricity shortages that have hindered economic growth in the country of 240 million people. (published 0019 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RENEWED ENERGY: OBAMA'S AGENDA BOOSTS LOBBYING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Obama administration's focus on renewable energy and energy efficiency has spurred a burst of lobbying, as an emerging class of energy companies races to win federal funding and shape legislation. (published 2010 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI FIN MIN: STRONG BAHT DUE TO TRADE SURPLUS, CAP INFLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The recent strengthening of the Thai baht is mainly due to a continued trade surplus and capital inflows, Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Wednesday. (published 0258 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NATL AUSTRALIA BK TO LAUNCH 5-YEAR A$ BOND - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 National Australia Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to launch and price a benchmark five-year Australian-dollar denominated bond Wednesday, market participants said. (published 0058 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Indian Media \par India Refiners Under-Recovery Loss This FY May Be INR250B - Business Standard \par Global Slowdown Hits Essar, Welspun SEZ Plans - Business Standard \par India Govt Refers Daimler Bid For Hero JV Stake To CCEA - PTI \par India Govt:States Can Only Levy Ctrl Sales Tax On Crude - The Hindu \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jet Airways\f28 \uc2 \f2  India Sacks Further 2 Pilots - PTI \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Essar Oil\f28 \uc2 \f2  To Submit Coal-Gas Devt Plan To Govt Soon - DNA Money \par Lanco Infra To Up Kondapalli Plant Ca