\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso rises on money inflows, rupiah NDFs fall\b0\par\par\uc2 702 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2009\par 09:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso firmed on Tuesday due to remittance inflows and firmer stocks, while the Singapore dollar inched up towards nine-month high hit the previous day amid fears of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Asian shares touched a one-year high while gold prices hit $1,000 an ounce for the first time in six months in a sign of investor concerns about the sustainability of the global economic recovery. [ID:nSP506640]\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> rose as far as 48.37 per dollar, up half of a percent from Friday's close, buoyed by remittance inflows during the long weekend. The market was shut on Monday for holiday.\par \par \uc2 "Accumulated inflows over the long weekend have pushed down dollar/peso today, aided also by the overall weak state of the dollar" said a dealer in Manila.\par \par \uc2 He added the peso was supported on the rise in Asian shares which attracted more fund inflows into the region.\par \par \uc2 "The global markets have embraced another round of risk appetite and have assumed further bullishness lead by the advance in gold prices," the dealer said.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> gained a fifth of a percent to 1.4310 per U.S. dollar but was held off its nine-month high at 1.4308 hit on Monday as investors fretted about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its strength.\par \par \uc2 "U.S. dollar/\b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is drifting lower as the euro getting paid up on the surge in gold," said a trader.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar has gained almost 9 percent against the dollar since early March, fanning fears among investors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might step in the market to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages Singapore dollar's nominal effective exchange rate (NEER) within a secret band.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> gained 0.6 percent to 10,000 per dollar, while dollar/rupiah non-deliverable forwards fell further although the past week's decline in one-month NDFs has brought them so close to the spot rate that scope for further tightening in forward points seems limited.\par \par \uc2 One-month dollar/rupiah NDFs <IDRNDFOR=> eased to 10,025, implying in a 0.2 percent rupiah depreciation from the spot.\par \par \uc2 "It's a better risk environment overall and it's one of the few countries where yields are still high. So there has been good client interest in bonds and short-term bills," said a trader in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "But at current levels it does seem a little overdone. Spot has gone from 12,000 to current 10,000, so people are looking to square their positions now," the trader added.\par \par \uc2 Spot rupiah traded close to 12,000 per dollar in March, and one-year NDFs were then pricing in a 16 percent rupiah depreciation. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at  0708 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        92.46          92.99       +0.57\par  Sing dlr        1.4297         1.4339       +0.29\par  Taiwan dlr      32.771         32.865       +0.29\par  Korean won     1229.80        1233.50       +0.30\par  Baht             34.02          34.03       +0.03\par  Peso             48.37          48.62       +0.52\par  Rupiah        10000.00       10055.00   