\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah rises on risk-taking, Sing dlr at 1-mth high\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2009\par 07:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 7 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah firmed on Monday as investors bought risky assets on optimism about the global economy, while Singapore dollar was boosted by news that Abu Dhabi's state fund ATIC would invest in a local chipmaker.\par \par \uc2 Asian stocks rose on Monday after better-than-expected U.S. jobs data on Friday reinforced optimism about economic recovery and a pledge by G20 leaders over the weekend to keep stimulus measures in place for longer. [IDnL7493885]\par \par \uc2 The Philippine markets were shut for holiday.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The high-yielding rupiah <IDR=> gained 0.6 percent to 10,050 per dollar, as investors bought local stocks <.JKSE>.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah, Asia's best performer this year with a gain of just over 9 percent against the dollar, is often the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice when investors increase risk.\par \par \uc2 "I think it's the story of the return of risk appetite," said Enrico Tanuwidjaja, strategist at \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank has raised its year-end rupiah forecast to 9,700 per dollar from 10,200 due to economic recovery and capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, one-month dollar/rupiah non-deliverable forwards <IDR1MNDFOR=> fell to 10,070, implying a 0.1 percent rupiah fall from the spot compared to 0.4 percent at Friday's close.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> gained half of a percent to 1.4315 per U.S. dollar, its highest in one month, after news that Abu Dhabi's state fund ATIC has offered to buy Singapore contract chipmaker Chartered Semiconductor for $1.8 billion. [ID:nSIN496807]\par \par \uc2 "Singapore dollar gained on the belief that ATIC will have to sell U.S. dollar and buy Singapore dollar to pay for the deal," said a trader.\par \par \uc2 Some traders suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, which has risen almost 9 percent against the U.S. dollar since early March due to optimism about the global economy.\par \par \uc2 Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steers policy by managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a secret trade-weighted band and many analysts believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is nearing the upper end of the band. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0519 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        93.14          92.99       -0.16\par  Sing dlr        1.4313         1.4390       +0.54\par  Taiwan dlr      32.837         32.905       +0.21\par  Korean won     1233.90        1241.50       +0.62\par  Baht             34.04          34.05       +0.03\par  Rupiah        10060.00       10110.00       +0.50\par  Rupee            48.74          48.88       +0.28\par  Ringgit         3.5160         3.5230       +0.20\par  Yuan            6.8293         6.8300       +0.01\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        93.14          90.60       -2.73\par  Sing dlr        1.4313         1.4340       +0.19\par  Taiwan dlr      32.837         32.860       +0.07\par  Korean won     1233.90        1259.50       +2.07\par  Baht             34.04          34.80       +2.23\par  Peso             48.64          47.52       -2.30\par  Rupiah        10060.00       11000.00       +9.34\par  Rupee            48.74          48