\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ruupiah rises, Singapore dlr eases on cbank jitters\b0\par\par\uc2 540 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2009\par 08:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 21 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah rose on Friday but later pared its gains in line with local stocks, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar eased on talk of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen surged to a one-month high against the dollar <JPY=> as traders remained worried about the potential for further weakness in Chinese shares and shied away from risky investments. [ID:nT253351]\par \par \uc2  The Philippine markets were closed for holiday.\par \par \uc2  RUPIAH\par \par \uc2  The rupiah <IDR=> gains 0.3 percent to 10,030 per dollar as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed broadly weaker while local stocks rose. It later pulled back to 10,040 as local stocks gave up earlier gains.\par \par \uc2   "It's also  becaue of a lot of short dollar covering ahead of the weekend," said a trader in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2  The rupiah, the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, is still up nearly 10 percent against the dollar so far this year.\par \par \uc2  Indonesian shares <.JKSE> edged up in early trade, but later pulled back in tandem with Chinese stocks <.SSEC>.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, three-month dollar/rupiah NDFs <IDRNDFOR=> fall to 10,190, implying a 1.7 percent rupiah fall from the spot compared to 2 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> fell almost 0.3 percent to 1.4451 per U.S. dollar amid talk of possible official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.\par \par \uc2  One trader cited suspected U.S. dollar-buying at 1.4365-70 via an agent bank.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has gained nearly 8 percent since early March and most analysts believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is close to the upper end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's secret trade-weighted band, fanning speculation that it may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its strength.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which lowered the mid-point of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in April in an effort to support the economy, is widely expected to keep its zero appreciation stance in October.  CURRRENCIES VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0626 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        93.69          94.19       +0.53\par  Sing dlr        1.4434         1.4408       -0.18\par  Taiwan dlr      32.933         32.966       +0.10\par  Korean won     1249.50        1246.90       -0.21\par  Baht             34.00          34.01       +0.03\par  Rupiah        10040.00       10060.00       +0.20\par  Rupee            48.74          48.70       -0.07\par  Ringgit         3.5255         3.5250       -0.01\par  Yuan            6.8318         6.8318       +0.00\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        93.69          90.60       -3.30\par  Sing dlr        1.4434         1.4340       -0.65\par  Taiwan dlr      32.933         32.860       -0.22\par  Korean won     1249.50        1259.50       +0.80\par  Baht             34.00          34.80       +2.35\par  Peso             48.40          47.52       -1.82\par  Rupiah        10040.00       11000.00       +9.56\par  Rupee            48.74          48.7