\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Singapore dollar firms, baht again capped by c.bank\b0\par\par\uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2009\par 08:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Singapore dollar edges up, buoyed by capital inflows\par \par \uc2 * Thai baht attempts go higher but c.bank keeps it on leash\par \par \uc2 * Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  move in tight ranges in slow trade\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 14 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar edged up on Friday amid signs of capital inflows, while the Thai baht's rise was contained by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar hit an 11-month high against the dollar after Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens hinted at higher interest rates [ID:nSYD342603], but most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved in narrow ranges in tandem with stocks.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=TH> gained a third a percent to 33.95 per dollar but was repeatedly pushed back to the weaker side of the 34 level by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has almost become a daily routine.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  has been closely guarding the psychologically important 34 level in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar/baht is under selling pressure, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps buying dollars," said a Bangkok-based trader.\par \par \uc2 The baht has gained almost 7 percent since early March, in line with its regional peers buoyed by optimism about a recovery in the global economy.\par \par \uc2 The baht's rise came to a halt in June as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequentely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shackle the unit within a tight 33.9-34.3 range for fear that a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hurt the already ailing export sector.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> gained a fifth of a percent to 1.44 per U.S. dollar, but its strength was capped by worries about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investors have been fearful of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, which has risen almost 8 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early March, even though the island's economy has only showed modest recovery from a deep recession.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steers monetary policy by managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a trade-weighted band and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be warranted if the unit breaches the upper end of the secret band.\par \par \uc2 Wei Zheng Kit, economist at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , said the Singapore dollar has been underpinned by a return of net capital inflows into the country since May, which pushed up asset prices.\par \par \uc2 "Capital inflows have pushed the Singapore dollar's nominal effective exchange rate (NEER) towards its strong side of the policy band since mid-April," he said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Kit reckoned that Singapore dollar's NEER has been hovering more than 100 basis points above the mid-point of the band.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased policy by lowering the mid-point of the band in April help the economy. The bank is widely expected to keep its neutral stance when it reviews policy in October.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day at   0621 GMT\par  \f28 \b \h